ed_matrix = [[matrix[i][j] * idf[j] for j in range(cols)] for i in range(rows)]\n\nNeed to import math.\n\nBut the task says may use only Python standard library, so math is fine.\n\nReturn dict with keys 'idf', 'row_degree', 'weighted_matrix'.\n\nNote: The payload also has '_case_nonce' but we ignore it.\n\nEdge: matrix might be empty? But fixture shows 6x5.\n\nThus implement solve function.\n\nWe must output a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing Python source as a string, properly escaped. Also ensure no extra text.\n\nWe'll produce the code with proper indentation and escape for JSON.\n\nLet's write the Python code as:\n\nimport math\n\ndef solve(case):\n    matrix = case['matrix']\n    rows = len(matrix)\n    if rows == 0:\n        cols = 0\n    else:\n        cols = len(matrix[0])\n    idf = []\n    for j in range(cols):\n        df = sum(1 for i in range(rows) if matrix[i][j] != 0)\n        if df == 0:\n            idf.append(0.0)\n        else:\n            idf.append(math.log(rows / df))\n    row_degree = [sum(row) for row in matrix]\n    weighted_matrix = [\n        [matrix[i][j] * idf[j] for j in range(cols)]\n        for i in range(rows)\n    ]\n    return {\n        'idf': idf,\n        'row_degree': row_degree,\n        'weighted_matrix': weighted_matrix\n    }\n\nNote: Use math.log for natural log.\n\nNow need to wrap as JSON string with escaped newlines, quotes, backslashes.\n\nWe'll produce final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1136,"completion_tokens":1384,"total_tokens":2520,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1024},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1165},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1024,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":112},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}